unny  well i'm not funny at all you're pretty  funny mark's very funny  but russian everybody's fun what was it  about rush  and the answer is who the hell knows he  was just  unbelievably special and sean one thing  again you've been in radio a long  long time from the local level to one of  the biggest radio hosts in the world  everybody dials it in once or twice  everybody  in radio you're sick you don't feel good  you take a lot of calls whatever it may  be  not rush and if he did it you could  never tell  i never listened to i would listen on  apps i'd go to wrestlingbar.com  i'd listen on the wcbm app wmal wherever  i was and i'm telling you  i never heard a time where i could tell  you all right  today he's dialing it in not once in 20  plus years and we all remember the first  time  we heard rush limbaugh and sadly i  remember the last time too  december 23rd and if i only would have  known as i was listening i was actually  brushing my teeth listening on december  23rd  in my bathroom that those were the last  moments that we were going to hear rush  limbaugh on the radio  you know i would have treated those  moments a little differently sean  yeah i uh i think we all would have i  mean  i don't think the country ever took them  for granted you know it's funny because  after every political cycle  and and russia experience this a lot too  he started when reagan was president was  there for bush 41  eight years of clinton mary matlin said  and i mentioned this  uh with harris faulkner and bill hemmer  earlier today  um you know mary matlin said well  how would we have survived without rush  during that years because he lifted  everybody up  well then that resulted in in three led  to  uh obama then we had donald trump and  now we have somebody  who's cognitively struggling um  and you know you think about it people  would always say well  what's rush going to talk about now  democrats elected or what's  what are you guys in talk radio going to  talk about no